The greatest common divisor of two whole numbers, by Euclid's method. The input is the pair (a . b). The gcd of 0 and 0 is 0. The output is Ok of the gcd, or Err if a remainder fails.
---

---
fn p
	letrec g = fn (a b)
		if (= b 0)
			(Ok a)
		else
			let r = ((% a b)?)
			(g b r)
	(g (fst p) (snd p))
---
⟨12 18⟩ => Ok 6 fuel 1000
⟨7 13⟩ => Ok 1 fuel 1000
⟨0 5⟩ => Ok 5 fuel 1000
⟨9 0⟩ => Ok 9 fuel 1000
⟨100 75⟩ => Ok 25 fuel 1000

